Draw one CDC run, including the branches that refuse

Section 4.4 described the notebook as a code sketch, which reads well
once you already know the shape and poorly otherwise. The new diagram
shows the whole run: the paging loop, the three ways it can be
interrupted, and the two places it declines to write rather than write
something wrong.

Colour carries meaning rather than decoration. Reads are teal, writes
blue, the snapshot seed violet, refusals red, and the best-effort
acknowledgement amber - so the two red terminals stand out as the
deliberate dead ends they are.

The three notes under it are the invariants the picture exists to make
obvious: `from` is exclusive, the watermark is written after the data,
and a RESET cannot be replayed because the log holds no rows for it.
Each of the three has been violated at least once in this repository,
and each violation was silent.

Verified by parsing every Mermaid block in the document with Mermaid 11
rather than by eye.

